# Death in the test playground costs nothing (#321.3): the hero dies and is back at the playground's start at once,
# alive with full life, in GAMEPLAY and the same area - no death screen, no menu, no load. Until that is built, death
# shows the game's death screen: life stays 0 and the state leaves GAMEPLAY, so the waits and asserts below fail.
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 playground-respawn
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -Playground -VrSim idle -Sequence playground-respawn
# How the hero is killed: the script console's `poison 100000` (ARX_PLAYER_Poison, src/game/Player.cpp). It needs no
# second entity - `<npc>.dodamage player N` does, and a self-inflicted dodamage does nothing (docs/vr/TESTING.md) - and
# no knowledge of the playground's NPC id. The poison's saving throw (resistPoison) is random, so the line is sent
# several times in one batch; the first frame after a success ARX_PLAYER_FrameCheck turns the huge poison into damagePlayer
# and the game raises the `player.death` event (src/game/Damage.cpp), which the sequence waits for before it judges.
# The start is not hard-coded: the position at the start of the run is what the respawn must come back to (the
# generator's HERO_START, scripts/dev/playground/layout.mjs: the room's centre 8000/8000, 250 units from it).
# Not covered here (owner / verifier steps, they need another level): death in an original level is unchanged - launch
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Save mvp-goblin-fight -Sequence <a copy of this file without @playground,
#   with @save mvp-goblin-fight and @args --loadslot 0 and a `setplayercontrols on` line>
# and expect the death screen (state not GAMEPLAY, life 0, no respawn), as before the change.
@sim idle
@playground

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert area eq 30
@assert player.freelook eq true             # a --loadlevel start is in freelook in VR (#394): the inventory closed
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq false
@remember lifemax player.lifeMax
@remember startx player.x
@remember starty player.y
@remember startz player.z
@assert player.life gt 0
@assert player.mana ge 0

# 1. Away from the start (the room's middle, 200 units east; setpos takes the EYE: floor y 0 - 170 = -170), as the
# hero would be after a fight
setpos 8200 -170 8000 0
@frames 30
@assert player.x ge 8150
@assert player.x le 8250
@assert player.life gt 0

# 2. Dead: the hero's life goes to 0 (the death event is the proof it happened; the respawn may follow within frames)
poison 100000; poison 100000; poison 100000; poison 100000; poison 100000; poison 100000; poison 100000; poison 100000
@until events.byName."player.death" ge 1 15s

# 3. Within 3 s: alive again, full life, the same level, in GAMEPLAY, back at the start (the 200 units walked away undone)
@until player.life ge {lifemax} 3s
@assert state eq GAMEPLAY
@assert area eq 30
@assert menuMode eq ingame
@assert player.life ge {lifemax}
@assert player.mana gt 0
@assert player.x ge {startx-40}
@assert player.x le {startx+40}
@assert player.z ge {startz-40}
@assert player.z le {startz+40}
@assert player.y ge {starty-60}
@assert player.y le {starty+60}
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false

# 4. And it stays so: the poison is gone (the hero does not die again), the level is still the playground
@frames 90
@assert state eq GAMEPLAY
@assert area eq 30
@assert player.life ge {lifemax}
@assert events.byName."player.death" eq 1
@assert errors eq 0
